+    along with Moodle.  If not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.
+}}
+{{!
+    @template core/login_layout
+
+    Theme NTT override of the login-flow layout (login, forgot password, sign up, MFA, ...).
+
+    Core renders a split screen: a decorative left panel (background photo, "Welcome to Moodle" card, user/site/country
+    statistics) next to the form. NTT drops the left panel completely and shows only the form, as one card centred on
+    the page, with no image or icon of its own (the only picture that can appear is the site logo, if an administrator
+    has configured one). Nothing else changes: the form itself (core/loginform) and every form-related id, name and class are
+    untouched, so login behaviour, JavaScript and Behat selectors keep working.
+
+    Context variables required for this template:
+    * output - The core renderer output object (provides main_content).
+
+    Example context (json):
+    {
+        "output": {
+            "main_content": "<h1>Login form goes here</h1>"
+        }
+    }
+}}
+<div id="page-content" class="ntt-login">
+    <div id="region-main" class="ntt-login-main" role="main">
+        <div id="region-main-box" class="ntt-login-box">
+            <div class="login-container ntt-login-card">
+                {{{ output.main_content }}}
+            </div>
+        </div>
+    </div>
+</div>
